    <item>
      <title>The Descent of Bhishma</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In the city of Hastinapura, Bhishma, a legendary warrior and cousin of the Pandavas and Kauravas, vowed to never yield to any woman. Born with superhuman strength and unmatched martial prowess, Bhishma&apos;s pride is rooted in his unwavering dedication to duty and family honor. He fights alongside the Kauravas against the Pandavas in the Great War, refusing to take up arms against his own kin. However, when the Kaurava prince Duryodhana attempts to seize the throne, Bhishma is torn between his loyalty to his family and his duty to uphold justice. As the war rages on, Bhishma is forced to confront his own limitations and the true cost of his pride. He takes up arms against the Kauravas, ultimately killing many of his own kin. This is Pride — the rigid adherence to duty that blinds us to its own consequences. Can we recognize our own self-imposed boundaries, or do they consume us like the Kauravas&apos; hubris?</description>
